ULTIMATE LONG‑TERM BOUND 
--------------------------------
- 003 / 530.1	Theoretical limits, information/physics

This note presents a coherent physicalist/ultrafinitist view that every 
mathematical object has a finite maximum representational depth imposed by 
the information and computation capacity of the physical universe. The 
proposal presents a rigorous physicalist and ultrafinitist framework. By 
anchoring mathematical existence to representational and computational 
capacity, it bridges physical limits (quantum mechanics, general 
relativity, and thermodynamics) with formal mathematical foundations.

There exists a general physical maximum representational depth 𝑁_max, and 
this depth is the admission boundary for mathematical structures across 
numerical, algebraic, topological, computational, and relational domains.

Classical mathematical infinities are replaced by large but hard ceilings 
derived from quantum gravity, thermodynamics, and cosmology. Nobody has 
ever seriously tried to define an 𝑁_max limit across all mathematical 
structures as a unified admission criterion.

Classical math says:

  Definition ⇒ Object

Bounded math say:

  Definition ⇒ Specification  
  Specification ⇒ Representation  
  Representation ⇒ Must satisfy physical ceilings  
  Only then ⇒ Object

