Core claim
----------
All mathematical objects have a maximum representational depth determined 
by physical information and computation limits.

For any mathematical object M,

        M_Depth < f(I_max, Ops_max, L_P, t_P, ...)

where the arguments are fixed by the listed physical bounds. There are 
therefore no actual infinities and no unbounded potential infinities in 
any structure that can be represented or computed.

The position is a form of strict ultrafinitist applied to realizable 
representations count as legitimate mathematical objects. There are physical 
limits on representation and computation.

The physical ceilings
---------------------
Bekenstein bound and holographic principle correctly limit the 
information content of a region (or the observable universe) to roughly 
10^122 bits.

Lloyd bound limits the total number of operations the universe can
have performed to ~ 10^120.

Bremermann, Margolus–Levitin, and Landauer limits correctly constrain 
rates and energy cost of irreversible computation. Planck-scale cutoffs 
supply absolute floors on length, time, energy and action.

These are standard results in the literature of physical limits to
computation (Lloyd, Bekenstein, Bremermann, etc.). The order-of-
magnitude numbers for the observable universe are conventional and 
widely cited.

