I. PHYSICAL INFORMATION CEILINGS
--------------------------------
• Bekenstein Bound
        S ≤ (2π k R E) / (ħ c)
        → Max information in finite region.

   Notation:
   S   = entropy / information content (nats or bits)
   k_B = Boltzmann constant
   R   = radius of the region
   E   = total energy contained in the region
   ħ   = reduced Planck constant
   c   = speed of light

• Holographic Principle
        I_max ∝ A / (4 L_P^2)
        → Bits scale with AREA, not volume.

 HOLOGRAPHIC PRINCIPLE (Bekenstein-Hawking / covariant form)
   S ≤ A / (4 ℓ_P²)

   Notation:
   S    = maximum entropy
   A    = surface area of the boundary
   ℓ_P  = Planck length = √(ħ G / c³)
   G    = gravitational constant

• Cosmological Information Limit (observable universe)
        I_total ≈ 10^122 bits
        → Finite information in observable universe.

 INFORMATION LIMIT 
   I_univ ≲ 10¹²² bits
   (order-of-magnitude from horizon area / 4 ℓ_P²)

II. PHYSICAL COMPUTATION CEILINGS
---------------------------------

• Seth Lloyd Bound
        Ops_total ≤ 10^120
        → Max operations universe can perform.

 LLOYD BOUND (total operations the universe can perform)
   #ops ≤ (2 E t) / (π ħ)

   For the observable universe (order of magnitude):
   #ops ≲ 10¹²⁰

   Notation:
   E = total energy available
   t = age of the universe (or available time)

• Bremermann Limit
        Rate ≤ 10^50 bits/s/kg
        → Max computation rate per mass.

   Rate ≤ c² / h  ≈ 1.356 × 10⁵⁰ bits s⁻¹ kg⁻¹

   Notation:
   c = speed of light
   h = Planck constant

• Margolus–Levitin Bound
        τ_perp ≥ πħ / (2E)
        → Quantum speed limit for state transitions.

   MARGOLUS–LEVITIN BOUND (quantum speed limit)
   τ_⊥ ≥ (π ħ) / (2 E)

   Equivalent rate:
   ops/sec ≤ (2 E) / (π ħ)

   Notation:
   τ_⊥ = minimum time to reach an orthogonal state
   E   = average energy above ground state

• Entropy / Landauer Bound
        E_min = kT ln 2 per irreversible bit
        → Minimum energy cost of erasure.

 LANDAUER’S PRINCIPLE (entropy bound on irreversible computation)
   E_erase ≥ k_B T ln 2   per bit

   Notation:
   T = temperature of the heat bath

• Heat‑Death Limit
        → Computation halts as universe approaches thermal equilibrium.

