Key Theoretical Context
-----------------------
Del Santo & Gisin Connection: 
Fits directly alongside work on finite-precision classical mechanics. Gisin 
showed that classical determinism relies on the non-physical assumption that 
initial conditions store infinite bits of information. Capping real numbers 
via interval cutoffs restores operational indeterminism to classical physics.

Informational Completeness: 
In I_N, Cauchy sequences do not converge to an abstract limit point; they 
terminate once the interval width hits 10^-N. Completeness becomes a 
property of finite structural closure rather than infinite accumulation.

